From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:04:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: the V_MOVREL cases across the parts of 0085's local
 array, compiled or run on the GPU

Two cases index 192 registers (v10 up to v201), so the local array of
0085 has three parts: V_MOVRELS_B32 reads in the second and the third,
V_MOVRELD_B32 writes in the third while the registers of the other two
keep their values. --movrel-compile-only compiles and validates the
four V_MOVREL cases without the GPU; --movrel-only runs them on it,
with a harness that accepts robust storage accesses aligned to 4 bytes,
as RADV aligns them (the cases read and write whole dwords in bounds).
On the 780M (RADV, Mesa 26.1): the four pass, and a wrong expected
value fails with the values read.

The test binary did not build since GetGraphicsPipeline returns a
pointer: dereferenced where a reference is wanted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/ShaderRecompilerComputeTests.cpp | 81 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 78 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/ShaderRecompilerComputeTests.cpp b/tests/ShaderRecompilerComputeTests.cpp
index fcf06730..59e91108 100644
